{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1790588952","published":"2026-09-28T09:49:27Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:30:52.616514077Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-33818","CVE-2026-56858","CVE-2026-56859","CVE-2026-56860","CVE-2026-56862"],"summary":"podman: Fix of 5 CVEs","details":"- rebuild with newer golang version 1.22.9-1.el9_2.tuxcare.els26 to fix the\n  following Go standard-library CVE's\n  - CVE-2026-33818: encoding/asn1: enforce a maximum recursion depth in\n    parseField and parseSequenceOf, so a deeply nested crafted DER payload can\n    no longer exhaust the stack while unmarshalling\n  - CVE-2026-56858: html/template: keep the JavaScript regexp/division context\n    up to date across brace transitions, so pathological input can no longer\n    close an unescaped '/' early and inject arbitrary content\n  - CVE-2026-56859: encoding/xml: track unmarshal depth on the decoder stack\n    instead of a local counter that DecodeElement reset, so a custom\n    UnmarshalXML implementation can no longer bypass the depth limit\n  - CVE-2026-56860: net/url: resolve reference paths on a byte buffer with\n    index-based backtracking instead of rebuilding a string on every \"..\"\n    segment, removing the quadratic time and allocation cost\n  - CVE-2026-56862: crypto/tls: only treat application data, and handshake\n    records seen before the handshake completes, as state-advancing, so a peer\n    can no longer spam post-handshake KeyUpdate messages to force unbounded\n    key derivation","affected":[{"package":{"name":"podman","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/podman?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:4.4.1-13.el9_2.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1790588952.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-docker","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/podman-docker?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:4.4.1-13.el9_2.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1790588952.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-gvproxy","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/podman-gvproxy?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:4.4.1-13.el9_2.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1790588952.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-plugins","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/podman-plugins?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:4.4.1-13.el9_2.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1790588952.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-remote","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/podman-remote?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:4.4.1-13.el9_2.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1790588952.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-tests","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/podman-tests?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:4.4.1-13.el9_2.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1790588952.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://errata.tuxcare.com/els_os/almalinux9.2esu/CLSA-2026-1790588952.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33818"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.